sequenceDiagram
    participant Server
    participant Kernel
    participant Client
    
    Server->>Kernel: socket(AF_INET, SOCK_STREAM, 0)
    Kernel-->>Server: sockfd
    
    Server->>Kernel: bind(sockfd, address, port)
    Server->>Kernel: listen(sockfd, backlog)
    Note over Server: Ready to accept connections
    
    Server->>Kernel: accept(sockfd, ...) - blocks
    
    Client->>Kernel: socket(AF_INET, SOCK_STREAM, 0)
    Kernel-->>Client: sockfd
    
    Client->>Kernel: connect(sockfd, server_addr)
    Kernel->>Kernel: TCP 3-way handshake
    Kernel-->>Server: Connection established
    Kernel-->>Client: Connected
    
    Server->>Kernel: accept returns new_sockfd
    
    Client->>Server: send(sockfd, "GET /", ...)
    Server->>Client: send(new_sockfd, "HTTP/1.1 200", ...)
    
    Client->>Kernel: close(sockfd)
    Kernel->>Server: FIN
    Server->>Kernel: close(new_sockfd)
    
    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
        Note over Server,Client: TCP guarantees delivery, and ordering
    end
